{
  "version": 1,
  "_README": [
    "md-random-artefact, rebuilt declaratively in md-my-hown-mod.",
    "",
    "TWO RULES both the target mod forces, and both verified by running its",
    "own validators against this file:",
    "",
    "1. Ids are SUFFIXES. md-my-hown-mod namespaces every entry as",
    "   md-my-hown-mod:<suffix> (fullIdOf, src/ui/schema.ts:624) and its",
    "   ID_PATTERN contains no colon. The source mod's md-random-artefact:",
    "   ids cannot be spelled here at all, so they are renamed below. That is a",
    "   real difference from the source, not cosmetic: these structures do not",
    "   carry the original mod's id, and nothing else in that mod can find them.",
    "",
    "2. Data is stored as defaultData, NOT as the panel's dataFieldsJson list.",
    "   entryToForm only ever reads defaultData. A config that stores the list",
    "   instead imports cleanly and then registers an entry with no data at",
    "   all -- measured, not assumed; the list form reads back empty.",
    "",
    "3. A sprite id IS the structure id. render.imageName must equal a loaded",
    "   sprite id exactly or the structure draws nothing, and the two lists are",
    "   written in different places. Keeping them equal by hand is how this file",
    "   shipped a version where every material link pointed at a sprite that was",
    "   never loaded.",
    "",
    "ASSETS are copied into md-my-hown-mod/assets/artefact/ and referenced with",
    "`path` (mod-relative, resolved by loadFromMod) rather than `source` (an",
    "absolute file:// URL), which is only needed for another mod's files.",
    "terrain-collector.png is deliberately absent: the terrain generator is out",
    "of scope.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS HERE: 5 structures, 5 sprites, 9 buffer slots, 1 processing entry",
    "(the generator's tick), 3 signal senders (the material links), and the 4",
    "processes they name. All of it compiles.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS PINNED, and why: the source mod picks a RANDOM material per cycle",
    "and SEARCHES for a free cell to spawn an artefact in. This catalogue has no",
    "random action and no free-cell search, so this version is deterministic. The",
    "audit's section 3 says what that costs. The links read three separate",
    "links.*Active flags rather than comparing materialIndex, because the engine",
    "only asks a sender 'is this truthy' and 1 and 2 are both truthy.",
    "",
    "See random-artefact-audit.md for the full mapping and for the two things",
    "this config cannot do."
  ],
